TODO list (incomplete)

This is a Bestechnic BES2600 / BEST2002 SDIO mac80211 driver (CW1200-family
WSM firmware protocol).  On PineTab2 v2.0 (RK3566, mmc2) STA Wi-Fi works at
fdf13926e22c: firmware load, idle scan, open and WPA2 associate, DHCP, ping,
and switching between APs (STARLINK open, NETGEAR15 WPA2).  Bluetooth has
never worked.

The driver was previously removed from staging for quality.  Do not send it
upstream until the items below are addressed enough that timeouts and RF
misses cannot oops the machine or flood WARN stacks.

Test both APs, both directions, after every change.  First association after
boot is not enough.

Proven working (STA, PineTab2 v2.0, firmware Dec 2023, fdf13926e22c)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
* Probe, boot + main firmware, phy registration.
* STA + P2P_DEVICE vifs (P2P is host-only; see below).
* Idle scan: 2.4 GHz then 5 GHz, firmware scan-complete status 0.
* Open (STARLINK) and WPA2-CCMP (NETGEAR15) association, 4-way, DHCP, ping.
* Switching STARLINK ↔ NETGEAR15 after a working session.
* Do not force_close the SDIO bus on -EBUSY (hard-locks the SoC).

Do not regress those without a replacement that has been tested on hardware.

Broken commits (wifi-broken, do not replay as a lump)
-----------------------------------------------------
* 0d7099dbf846 rate-limit / weak-signal: NETGEAR15 still worked, STARLINK
  always failed.  The 1 Mbps clamp and related TX policy belong here.
* 26ee084ec255 same STARLINK-fail / NETGEAR-ok pattern.
* c426582bf6ff associated-scan: BACKGROUND + FORCE_BACKGROUND, no
  wsm_reset while STA.  Required for mainline — do not skip with
  -EBUSY.  Bare BACKGROUND of NM's 14+27 channels at 100 ms dwell
  while staying ACTIVE killed AMPDU.  Do not toggle BA 0/177
  around scan.
* d6c2ab442ff4 mainline-prep: broken.
* 147ad3eaca60 WARN_ON/BUG_ON: first connect after boot worked; later
  connects failed.  Do not re-apply that conversion blindly.

WARN_ON / BUG_ON
----------------
* Firmware NAK, SDIO timeout, and "AP did not ACK" must not WARN_ON
  (stack + TAINT_WARN) or BUG_ON (panic).  The 147ad3e conversion of
  those to bes_fail()/bes_err() broke reconnect; redo it in small
  tested hunks.
* Keep WARN_ON only for programmer invariants (NULL about to be
  dereferenced, queue id out of range).
* Easy BUG_ON pass (no I/O / TX-lock / queue-remove): unsupported
  set_key cmd, double hw_scan, SSID length, queueId>=4 and missing
  channel in work items, unknown SDD rev, missing DPD blob.  Leave
  wsm_cmd.ptr, tx_lock, queue.c, BH lengths, queue_remove for later.
* hwio.c: BUG_ON(!bes2600_subs_ops) → -ENODEV.
* bes2600_sdio.c: BUG_ON(!self/!bus_priv) → -ENODEV/-EINVAL/false.
* wsm.c (easy): unknown confirm id, wsm_buf_init already allocated.
  Still open: wsm_cmd.ptr, tx_lock, wait_event LAST_CHANCE, queue_remove.

Logging
-------
* Hot-path bes_info (per-channel scan, per-frame TX/RX) is too loud.
  Per-channel assoc 0x0007 is bes_devel.  Keep one line per hw_scan
  request and scan complete at info until PS/scan is settled.
* Firmware load still prints version/CRC at info; fine for now.
* Bind device logs to the SDIO function, not a NULL global_dev.

Power save / WSM 0x0010
-----------------------
* SUPPORTS_PS + SUPPORTS_DYNAMIC_PS.  cfg.ps=1 → FAST_PS (0x81)
  even when dyn_to=0 (this stack means "firmware owns idle", not
  legacy PS).  Idle period from BES2600_FASTPS_IDLE_TIME if set,
  else mac80211 timeout.  Cache then send 0x0010; do not wait for
  0x0809.  Do not wsm_set_pm() from BH/RX.
* STARLINK 2.4 GHz: 0x0010 0x81 got 0x0809 psm=0x1.  Assoc, DHCP,
  AMPDU worked.  Legacy 0x01 as session idle never got 0x0809.

Suspend / resume / shutdown
---------------------------
* Deep suspend removes the STA vif.  On resume, MCU wake fails
  for tens of seconds: bes2600_sdio_active failed / 
  pwr_device_exit_lp_mode, active mcu fail, then LMAC station-ID
  and add_interface recover.  Screen blank / console dead until
  power-button is this path, not DRM.  Fix bes_pwr / SDIO
  resume so mmc2 comes back without that retry storm.
* Poweroff after a dead SDIO (TX -16) hung NM/wpa 1–3 min:
  scan.lock busy-loop in bes2600_stop, deactive WARN_ON,
  sdio_tx_work re-queueing -EBUSY forever.  Stop must abort
  the scan with a timeout, mark the bus stale after a short
  -EBUSY streak, and not WARN_ON deactive failure.

Scan
----
* Associated scan is required.  BACKGROUND + FORCE_BACKGROUND,
  10/25 TU, one channel per 0x0007.  Keep TX locked for the
  whole request.  If idle is ACTIVE, wrap with legacy 0x01
  (cw1200); if already 0x01/0x81, skip the wrap.
* Never foreground 0x0007 while joined, never wsm_reset() on scan
  failure while STA.
* Do not run join_timeout/unjoin from scan first_run while associated.
* Drain once at start (do not drop the host count).  Skip 0x0008
  on associated scan timeout.  After that timeout, in_progress
  is 0 while AMPDU may still sit in firmware — the LMAC 3s
  monitor must not mark_bus_stale for leftover bufs (that
  refused 0x0006 and skipped every later scan).
* Drain can still leave bufs=20–46 after 500 ms when AMPDU is
  retrying (manual scan while ping/browser).  Info no longer
  prints that; leftover is devel.  Starting 0x0007 with a full
  window can still -110 — later item, not a dead bus.
* AMPDU RETRY_EXCEEDED can still show on STARLINK.

Association / rates / aggregation
---------------------------------
* 5 GHz STARLINK BSSIDs (ch36 / ch149 / :47: / :37:) fail auth
  at 6 Mbps.  2.4 GHz STARLINK (ch1, :27:) is the working BSS.
* EAPOL must not set data_acked or enable BA.  After STARLINK →
  NETGEAR, 4-way succeeded then minstrel/BA ran on the EAPOL ACK
  and data RETRY_EXCEEDED.  Stay on 1/6 Mbps until a non-EAPOL
  unicast data ACK, then BA (open and WPA2).
* Occasional first 4-way timeout on NETGEAR: M1 RX, then
  P53 drop st=9 (WSM_STATUS_NO_KEY_FOUND) — M3 encrypted before
  set_key installed the PTK.  NM retry / "connect" again works.
  Firmware already dropped the frame; host cannot decrypt it.
  Not an easy driver fix without LMAC buffering.
* Do not clamp ICMP/DNS/DHCP to 1 Mbps the way 0d7099 did until that
  change is re-proven against STARLINK.
* Firmware owns BlockAck.  Host ADDBA-Resp is dropped.  Do not
  auto-enable BA after HT ACKs ("connected" with 0% ping).
* Join with leftover hw_bufs_used: often 1 and expected (auth
  already in flight, or a scan/WSM slot after unjoin reset).
  prepare_for_join host-clears it; late confirms clamp underflow.
  Do not poke RX.  Do not queue_clear on unjoin.  Demote the
  bes_warn when we next touch that path; not a leak to chase now.
* wsm_reset drops the firmware TX rate-policy table.  Host cache must
  clear uploaded so MCS policies are sent again on the next BSS.

MAC / interfaces
----------------
* Stable MAC is derived from the SoC serial (02:00:00:3d:05:3c locally).
  Early dummy vs serial mismatch is confusing in dmesg; pick one story.
* P2P_DEVICE (nl80211 type 10) is host-only.  Do not send WSM on the
  STA if_id for it.  DanctNIX 6.15 disabled P2P_DEVICE; keep or drop
  explicitly.

Bluetooth
---------
* Never worked.  CONFIG_BES2600_BT is off.
* Makefile still lists bes2600_btusb.o; that file is not in the tree.
* /dev/bes2600 (bes_chardev) is leftover vendor userspace control.
  UART hciattach on ttyS1 is the distro workaround.

Hardware / firmware limits (not "just code")
--------------------------------------------
* PineTab2 does not wire BES2600 reset/power GPIOs the way the vendor
  EVB does.  A wedged chip needs a board power cycle.
* Firmware is proprietary (bes2600/best2002_fw_boot_sdio.bin +
  best2002_fw_sdio.bin, Dec 2023).  Fail cleanly if blobs are missing.
* Factory calibration comes from bes2600_factory.txt.

Kconfig / build
---------------
* Makefile is Kbuild-only (KERN_DIR / all: modules dropped).  Still has
  ccflags -Werror and hardcoded -DCHIP_WIFI_ROM_VER.
* Drop unused platform variants if PineTab2 is the only in-tree user,
  or isolate them.
* GET_MAC_ADDR_METHOD as int 1-4 is not kernel style.
* Android-style default paths (/data/applog/, /data/cfg/) do not belong
  in a generic driver.

Dead / leftover code
--------------------
* TODO:COMBO, HACK!!!, commented dump_stack(), #if 0, testmode / ITP.
* EPTA 0x0029 was a lockup source on a sick bus; do not pile it on
  join/unjoin without a proven need.  BT is unused.
* SDIO TX bounce (tx_pad): do not DMA padded length from the skb.

Lockups already hit (do not reintroduce)
----------------------------------------
* force_close on SDIO CTRL/CMD53 -EBUSY (hard lock CPU / kworker).
* Nested 0x0006 operational-mode while MCU wake failed.
* Scan WARN-loop of 0x0006 / 0x0007 / 0x0029 after a sick bus.
* Host-only unjoin after failed auth skipped wsm_reset; LMAC stayed
  joined; next 0x0007 returned status 13.

Not this driver
---------------
* rockchip-drm swiotlb buffer full.
* QSampleCache wireless-extensions warning.
* systemd-journald "Time jumped backwards".
* typec-extcon / husb311 (board patches, separate).
* Plasma/GNOME screen-blank policy; suspend itself is the driver
  (see Suspend / resume above).

Contact / trees
---------------
* Current development: branch wifi-good from fdf13926e22c.
  Tag wifi-good-fdf139 marks that snapshot.  Branch wifi-broken is the
  old tip (147ad3e) for reading diffs only.
* Distro: DanctNIX linux-pinetab2 on Codeberg
  (https://codeberg.org/DanctNIX/linux-pinetab2).
* Mainline: linux-staging / wireless, patches against linux-next, with
  this file kept honest as items close.
